        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Kamehameha I</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">c. 1736 CE – 1819 CE</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Born</span><span class="info-stat-val">Between 1736 and 1761 (c. 1736 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samuel-kamakau">Samuel Kamakau</a>'s widely accepted dating), by most accounts in Ainakea, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kohala-hawaii">Kohala, Hawaii</a>; son of Kekuʻiapoiwa II and Keōua Kalanikupuapa'ikalaninui, a descendant of Keawe through his mother</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Died</span><span class="info-stat-val">May 8 or 14, 1819, at Kamakahonu, the compound he built in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kailua-kona">Kailua-Kona</a>, where he spent his last years; his body was hidden and his resting place remains unknown</span></div>
